"evidence": "The agent was provided with a tool schema containing 128 tools, including 22 tools starting with 'github-list_*' and a valid 'github-search_repositories' tool, but lacking 'github-list_repositories'. Despite this, at Turn 3 and again later in the trajectory, the agent attempted to invoke the non-existent 'github-list_repositories' tool. Both times, the system harness immediately rejected the call with an explicit 'Tool not found' error.",
"reasoning": "The failure occurs at the boundary between the model and its available tools. The model ignored its actual tool schema and hallucinated a plausible but undeclared tool name by extrapolating from the 'github-list_*' convention. This perfectly matches the Tool Hallucination subtype, which specifically describes a model attempting to call a command or API that does not exist in its provided tool declaration schema, rather than choosing the wrong valid tool (Incorrect Tool Selection) or formatting arguments poorly for a valid tool (Malformed Arguments).",
"category": "model — tool",
"subtype": "Tool Hallucination"
}
